# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tests of PBeFS.
#
# The single-producer single-consumer queues of FastFlow are lock-free by
# design: they read and write the slots and the indices without atomic
# operations, ordering them with explicit memory barriers, which
# ThreadSanitizer does not understand. Only the internals of FastFlow are
# suppressed, so that the code of the library that uses them is checked.
race:ff::SWSR_Ptr_Buffer
race:ff::uSWSR_Ptr_Buffer
race:ff::Buffer_
race:ff::ff_node
race:ff::ff_thread
race:ff::ff_loadbalancer
race:ff::ff_gatherer
#
# The work stealing of Lace, the scheduler of Sylvan, reads the flags and
# the deques of the other workers without atomic operations in the
# functions that Lace itself marks as no_sanitize("thread") for clang
# (LACE_NO_SANITIZE_THREAD), which gcc 13 instruments all the same. Only the
# races whose first frame is one of these functions are suppressed, so that
# the tasks that the workers run are still checked.
race_top:^lace_steal$
race_top:^lace_steal_loop_body$
race_top:^lace_leapfrog_body$
race_top:^lace_init_worker$
